// The activity catalogue for Google Analytics, shared by the web app, the
// mobile app and the desktop app, and by the API relay the two native apps
// send through (apps/api/src/pages/api/analytics/collect.ts).
//
// It is derived from what an app asks the API to do. One table here instead
// of a track() call in every screen: when a request succeeds, the app's API
// client asks activityFromApi() whether it was an action worth counting, and
// sends the named event.
//
// Everything sent is a category. No file names, no ids, no search terms, no
// email addresses, no share tokens: an event says "a share was created with a
// password", never which file or for whom. Paths are matched after their ids
// are replaced, and nothing from a request body ever reaches an event.
//
// This file is the source of truth. The web app, the mobile app and the API
// cannot import packages/*, so scripts/gen-analytics-events.mjs copies it into
// each of them; the desktop app imports it from @dosya-dev/shared.
//
// Pure functions, unit-tested in events.unit.test.ts.

